{
  "concept": "A UV absorption spectrum identifies λmax as the wavelength where a compound absorbs most strongly, with 1,3-butadiene showing its diagnostic maximum near 217 nm and only weak absorption at longer wavelengths.",
  "figureType": "line_plot",
  "elements": [
    "plot area with pale pink-to-white vertical gradient background",
    "x-axis labeled 'Wavelength (nm)' spanning 200 to 400 nm",
    "x-axis tick marks and labels at 200, 220, 240, 260, 280, 300, 320, 340, 360, 380, and 400",
    "magenta right-pointing arrow following the x-axis label",
    "y-axis labeled 'Absorbance' spanning 0 to 1.0",
    "y-axis tick marks and labels at 0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8, and 1.0",
    "magenta upward-pointing arrow beside the y-axis label",
    "single magenta absorption curve for 1,3-butadiene",
    "rounded absorption maximum near 217 nm just below 0.9 absorbance",
    "annotation text 'λmax = 217 nm' positioned above and slightly right of the peak",
    "low nearly horizontal absorbance tail extending beyond 250 nm toward 400 nm",
    "movable marker dot on the absorption curve",
    "live wavelength and absorbance readout beside the marker",
    "peak-region highlight centered around 217 nm",
    "tail-region highlight over wavelengths beyond about 250 nm"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "wavelengthScan",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Wavelength",
      "range": [
        200,
        400,
        1
      ],
      "default": 217,
      "teaches": "λmax is not just the tallest point on the drawing; it is the wavelength value where the absorbance readout reaches its highest value as the spectrum is scanned"
    },
    {
      "id": "viewFocus",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "View focus",
      "options": [
        "Peak-only",
        "Full-tail"
      ],
      "default": "Peak-only",
      "teaches": "The important UV signal for 1,3-butadiene is concentrated near the short-wavelength peak, while the long-wavelength tail contributes little absorbance"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Find the maximum",
      "narration": "Start with the marker at the crest of the magenta curve. The absorbance readout is highest near 217 nm, so this wavelength is labeled λmax.",
      "state": {
        "wavelengthScan": 217,
        "viewFocus": "Peak-only"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Scan away from the crest",
      "narration": "Move the wavelength slider to the right and watch the dot drop rapidly down the curve. The absorbance falls sharply after the maximum, showing why nearby wavelengths are not λmax.",
      "state": {
        "wavelengthScan": 240,
        "viewFocus": "Peak-only"
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Compare the long tail",
      "narration": "Switch to the full-tail view and scan through longer wavelengths. Beyond about 250 nm, the curve is nearly flat and close to the baseline, so the diagnostic absorption is the short-wavelength peak rather than the tail.",
      "state": {
        "wavelengthScan": 320,
        "viewFocus": "Full-tail"
      }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "λmax is the wavelength at the highest absorbance point, and for 1,3-butadiene that point is the isolated peak near 217 nm rather than the weak long-wavelength tail.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Recreate the figure as a clean 2D line plot with a pale pink gradient filling the plotting rectangle, darkest near the top and fading toward white near the bottom. Use black axes and ticks, serif-style tick labels, and a bright magenta trace. The curve should begin near moderate absorbance at 200 nm, rise steeply to a smooth rounded crest near 217 nm just under 0.9, fall quickly by about 240 nm, then continue as a very low, gently declining tail to 400 nm. Place the 'λmax = 217 nm' annotation just above and to the right of the crest. In Peak-only mode, visually emphasize the peak with a subtle glow or shaded band around 217 nm while de-emphasizing the tail; in Full-tail mode, show the whole curve and lightly highlight the low tail beyond about 250 nm. The slider marker should be a small high-contrast dot riding exactly on the curve with a compact live readout such as 'λ = 217 nm, A ≈ 0.86'."
}

